  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nPatchy fog is expected to develop east of Rosebud County this \nmorning with the best chances being in Carter and Fallon Counties.\nThis is expected to dissipate by the late morning hours. \nSoutheast winds gusting into the 30s mph will continue for Carter\nand Fallon Counties today with winds decreasing throughout the \nevening. \n\nAbove average temperatures in the 50s and 60s F and dry \nconditions are expected through Monday. A pattern change to cooler\nand wetter conditions is expected during the middle to late week \nperiod. Models are in good agreement that an upper level wave will\nmove through the region Tuesday/Wednesday bringing 50-80% \nprecipitation chances. The chance for greater than 0.25 inches of \nprecipitation is 40-80% with the highest chances being over the \nmountains and foothills. Snow is likely for the mountains but \nprecipitation type over the lower elevations is still uncertain \nwith both rain and snow being possible. \n\nAnother 500 mb wave is likely late next week, though\nthere is less agreement in what this one will look like. Some\nmodels are indicating an open wave while others are showing a\nclosed off upper level low. It is not clear at this time which\nsolution would bring higher precipitation values. The chance for\nlower elevation snow will be greater with this second system as\nhigh temperatures decrease from the 40s and 50s F Tuesday to the \n30s and 40s F by late week. Torgerson",
